{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["It should not seem hard to you — that you send him free from you with what you give him as a double portion — the wages of a hired worker — for the service of six years that he served you, that you grant him from your flock and from your threshing floor and from your winepress, besides the hired-service value of the six years in which you acquired him, for therefore YHWH will bless you in all that you do. Now the interpretation of this verse is like ״ולא ירע לבבך בתתך לו״, and likewise ״תרע עינה באיש חיקה ובבנה ובבתה״ — giving to one of them, for an evil eye and hardness of heart speak of giving money to others. What they are accustomed to explain, that לא יקשה בעינך refers to your sending him free at the end of six, since he served you many — six — years, meaning more than other hired workers, is foolishness in my view. For why should it seem hard to him to send him free? Did he not acquire him originally only for the service of six years, which everyone knows ends in the seventh? And furthermore, he should not have said משנה שכר שכיר but rather משנה שכיר? Some interpreters say: משנה שכיר — six years are, since an unspecified שכיר means three years, as written: ״בשלש שנים כשני שכיר ונקלה כבוד מואב״. This too is nonsense, for elsewhere it is written: ״בעוד שנה כשני שכיר״ — the meaning of כשני שכיר is three years specified, like כשני שכיר which is one year specified."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase שוטות הוא בידם rendered 'is foolishness in my view'; 'in their hands' may refer to what they hold as interpretation, but the idiom is uncertain and the translation is literal."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:04.417664812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}